§ `Schedule 1 paragraph 2`

#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 2(1) guilty of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` `fish taken from private water`
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 2(1) guilty of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` `fish in public water`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 2(1) guilty of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` `fish in private water, nothing taken or destroyed`)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 2(1) liable on summary conviction for taking or destroying fish` `fish taken from private water` EQUALS `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `expected summary level 5 fine only`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 2(1) liable on summary conviction for taking or destroying fish` `fish in public water` EQUALS `no offence under this section on these facts`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 2(3) the court may order forfeiture of the thing he had with him` `fish convicted, tackle with him`
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 2(3) the court may order forfeiture of the thing he had with him` `fish not convicted, tackle with him`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 2(3) the court may order forfeiture of the thing he had with him` `fish convicted, tackle was not for fishing`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 2(3) the court may order forfeiture of the thing he had with him` `fish convicted of something else, tackle with him`)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 2(4) any person may arrest him without warrant` `fish arrest, caught in the act`
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 2(4) any person may arrest him without warrant` `fish arrest, no reason`)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 2(4) any person may seize the thing from him` `fish seizure, caught in the act, liable to forfeiture`
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 2(4) any person may seize the thing from him` `fish seizure, caught in the act, not liable to forfeiture`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 1 para 2(4) any person may seize the thing from him` `fish seizure, no reason, liable to forfeiture`)

